     "definition": "The specialization relationship represents that an element is a particular kind of another element.",
     "scopeNote": "The specialization relationship has been inspired by the generalization relationship in UML class diagrams but is applicable to specialize a wider range of concepts.\nA specialization relationship is always allowed between two elements of the same type.\nAlternatively, a specialization relationship can be expressed by nesting the specialized element inside the generic element.\n In this case, the “Take Out Travel Insurance” and “Take Out Luggage Insurance” processes are a specialization of a more generic “Take Out Insurance” process.",
