     "predicate": "triggers",
     "predicateLabel": "Triggers",
     "predicateDefinition": "Indicates a temporal or causal relationship between elements.",
     "notation": "t",
     "parent": "",
     "definition": "The triggering relationship represents a temporal or causal relationship between elements.",
     "scopeNote": "The triggering relationship is used to model the temporal or causal precedence of behavior elements in a process. The interpretation of a triggering relationship is that some part of the source element should be completed before the target element can start (see also Section 5.3.3, “Semantics of Dynamic Relationships”). Note that this does not necessarily mean that one behavior element actively starts another; in a hypothetical daily process, the “Have Lunch” activity follows (is triggered by) the “Have Breakfast” activity, even though there is no active signal between the two.\n",
